Autaschas Matt Gray.```   Note: The term "Aufkleber" translates to "stickers" or "labels" in English. However, in Romansh, there isn't a direct equivalent for "Aufkleber". The term "autaschas" is used for stickers or labels in Romansh. "Matt Gray" is a color name and can be translated as "grisch matt" in Romansh. So, the translation would be "Autaschas grisch matt". But if you're referring to a specific product or brand name, it might be best to keep it as "Matt Gray" and add a description in Romansh if necessary.   So, the most accurate translation would be:  ```Autaschas Matt Gray.```   If you're referring to a product or brand, you might want to keep the name as is and add a description in Romansh. For example:  ```Autaschas Matt Gray - Autaschas gratuitas.```   This would translate to "Matt Gray stickers - free stickers".
